{27} Says the Exalted, informing about the state of the polytheists on the Day of Resurrection and their being brought to the Fire: {And if you could see when they are made to stand before the Fire}: to be rebuked and reproached. You would see a terrifying matter and a dreadful state, and you would see how they acknowledged against themselves their disbelief and wickedness, and wished that they could be returned to the world, {and they will say, "Oh, would that we could be returned, and not deny the signs of our Lord, and be among the believers."}

{28} {Rather, there will have appeared to them what they had been concealing before}: for they used to conceal within themselves that they were liars, and it would appear in their hearts at many times, but corrupt aims prevented them from that and turned their hearts away from good. They are liars in this wish, and their intention in it is only to ward off punishment from themselves. Had they {been returned, they would return to what they were forbidden, and indeed they are liars}.

{29} {And they said}, denying the Resurrection: {There is nothing but our life of this world}; that is: what is the reality of the matter, and the purpose of our existence is nothing but this worldly life alone, {and we will not be resurrected.}

